<p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">EDCO covers most of Escondido residential. They offer <strong>2 free bulky item pickups per year</strong> to residential customers. If it's one mattress or one couch and you can wait a week or two, schedule through EDCO first. Save the $125 for the bigger jobs.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold mb-2">Fire zone disposal</h3>
<p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Parts of East Escondido and the backcountry are in the CAL FIRE SRA (State Responsibility Area). Brush clearance, defensible-space debris, old wood fencing — we take it and route it to the county green waste facility. If you're under a 100-foot clearance notice from CAL FIRE, we can work fast to help you come into compliance.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold mb-2">HOA and gated communities</h3>
<p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Hidden Meadows, Champagne Village, the Country Club. Most gated communities require a COI (certificate of insurance) naming the HOA as additional insured before crews enter. Give us the HOA name and we'll have the COI emailed ahead of arrival.</p>
</div>
</div>
